      {
        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "The spec for #26: \"配对升级两段式+指纹呈现：扫码+人在电脑端输码双确认（手机绝不代确认）；设备凭据指纹人眼可核；键变更 fail-closed\" — source dsh-Go.\n\nBut the user's §四 says \"配对设备指纹（人眼可核）+ 键变更 fail-closed 标记\" — not the two-stage pairing (that would require mobile-side changes). Since 手机端 is another repo, and §四 is in this batch (server side only), we implement the fingerprint + fail-closed marker here.\n\nWhat does \"键变更 fail-closed 标记\" mean concretely? Possibly: each device record stores a fingerprint derived from (deviceId, tokenHash). If the stored file's deviceId/tokenHash pair is tampered with / changed externally (i.e., the fingerprint doesn't match), mark the device as failed-closed (revoke/refuse) rather than trusting it. That is: store a `fingerprint` field computed as sha256(deviceId + tokenHash); on load, recompute and compare — mismatch → mark `integrityOk: false` and refuse token verification (fail-closed). That's a plausible reading: \"键变更\" = key material change in the store file.\n\nAlternative reading: phone presents (deviceId, token); if deviceId matches a record but token hash doesn't → key changed → mark device `keyMismatchAt` and fail-closed (403) until re-pair. This is \"键变更 fail-closed 标记\": a marker (in device record + exposed in API) that this device's key changed, and verified false.\n\nGiven the server-side-only constraint and \"标记\" (marker), I think the second reading is most actionable: add optional `deviceId` header/body on verification? But verifyDeviceToken is called by middleware with only token. Let me check index.ts auth middleware lines 200-260."
      }
    ],
