        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "No phone-side client in repo. So §一 must be a server-side belt-and-braces + phone-facing preflight. Let me reconsider the phrase in the user's summary: \"§一 手机 worker 执行前重验（取消后不产生副作用，单测钉死）\".\n\n\"执行前重验\" = re-verify before execution. Since the phone executes (not the server), the only true way is a phone-side check. But since phone repo isn't here, the batch can only add:\n(a) server endpoints/behavior that the phone will call, and/or\n(b) server-side guarantees at hand-off and result-write.\n\nGiven batch 25's own wording \"在 dispatch() 真该发出前，再查一次\" and \"在收结果写回前再查一次\" + \"开关 PHONE_ENSURE_ACTIVE\" + \"单测：取消后不发出 / 超时后不发出 / 已认领不重复发 / 取消后结果被丢弃 / 开关旁路\", this is clearly server-side in phone-worker.ts. And the tests are all about the server's delivery/result path. Even if some checks are redundant with existing `finish()` cleanup, adding explicit re-checks is cheap and makes the invariant explicit — that's what \"钉死\" means.\n\nFine — I'll implement exactly per batch 25 §3 (which is this batch's §一). To make the switch and tests meaningful, I'll structure it so:\n\n- `PendingEntry` keeps `deadlineAt` + `signal`.\n- `isEntryActive(entry, now)` → reason null | \"canceled\" | \"expired\" | \"claimed\".\n- Hand-off path `takeReadyTask()`: pops ready, drops entries that are gone or inactive (with finish), returns first active. Called only when PHONE_ENSURE_ACTIVE is on; else old `nextQueuedTask`.\n- Delivery: `flushPoll` iterates polls? Keep simple: only hand off to the first poll, but re-check there too.\n- Result path: check active; if inactive → discard, log id only, return 200 {ok:true, applied:false}; if switch off → old behavior (404 when missing, but if entry exists but expired-before-cleanup... old behavior would resolve). Difference observable by having abort fire *after* the timer? No—finish removes.\n\nTo make the switch genuinely observable, define \"inactive\" to include an explicit canceled set: add `canceledTasks: Set<string>` marked on abort, and keep it briefly. Hmm, overkill.\n\nAlternative meaningful difference: **timeout boundary**. Old: timer fires and removes. New: also check `Date.now() >= deadlineAt` at hand-off, so a task that is past deadline but whose timer hasn't fired yet (event loop blocked / timer clamped) is not delivered. This is genuinely non-redundant under event-loop lag, and testable by mocking? Hard to test deterministically.\n\nSimplest testable difference: at hand-off, if `entry.deadlineAt <= Date.now()` drop. With budgetMs=1 and a poll after 5ms, timer will have fired anyway. Deterministic tests are what matter, not switch observability. The switch test can assert that with `PHONE_ENSURE_ACTIVE=false` the behaviors still hold (bypass path) — i.e., canceled still rejected due to listener, result still 404. That satisfies \"开关旁路\" without contriving.\n\nHmm, but a switch that changes nothing is a lie per AGENTS (\"新能力给回滚开关\" + \"mock 不许空转\"). Let me design a real, observable new behavior that the switch gates:\n\nNew behavior: **hand-off gate (`deliverableReason`)**. Add an in-memory `abortedTasks: Set<string>` populated in onAbort *before* pending deletion, so we can distinguish \"canceled\" from \"unknown\" at result time and log it. But observationally at hand-off, if the abort fired, the entry is gone → nothing delivered either way. Same.\n\nNew behavior that is genuinely new and switchable: **task lease** — when handed to a poll, mark `entry.deliveredAt`; refuse a second delivery of the same taskId to a different device (already impossible). Not new.\n\nOK, alternative interpretation of §一 that yields real new behavior: \"已被别的 worker 认领\" — support **multiple devices polling concurrently**, where a task should be delivered to only one. Currently `flushPoll` takes the *first* poll entry regardless of device, and `ready` is a simple queue — already one delivery. But: if a poll's HTTP connection drops *after* delivery but before the phone gets it, the task is lost (in pending, not in ready, no retry). Not \"re-verify\" either.\n\nHonestly, the batch-25 spec is what the user wants (it's literally the same item). I'll implement the literal spec with explicit checks + a switch + tests, and in the change record honestly state that the existing `finish()` cleanup already covered most cases; the new gate makes it explicit and covers the event-loop-lag / post-resolve window, and that the switch is an exact rollback to today's code path.\n\nWait — there is one genuinely new, observable behavior: **result discarded after cancel, with an explicit log line and `applied:false` response instead of 404**. That's user-visible to the phone and satisfies \"取消后结果被丢弃（记一条日志）\". And at hand-off, a **stale-in-`ready` entry whose pending entry exists but whose signal aborted without listener firing**... \n\nHmm, actually here's a real one: today, `dispatch()` registers abort listener with `{once:true}` and `finish` removes from pending/ready. **But if the same taskId is dispatched twice** (retry/re-dispatch), the second `pending.set(taskId, ...)` overwrites the first entry, while the first promise is still pending and its timer will later call `finish` → `pending.delete(taskId)` — deleting the *second* entry! That's a real bug: the old task's timeout kills the new task's delivery. And \"已被别的 worker 认领\" ~ duplicate taskId. `newTaskId()` includes random hex so collision unlikely, but re-dispatch with same id is plausible. Fix: `finish` should only delete if `pending.get(taskId) === entry`. That is a genuine correctness fix under \"执行前重验 / 不重复\". Good — I'll include that guard and test it (duplicate dispatch same taskId: old timeout must not kill the new one).\n\nOK. Now §四 pairing. And §二 group endpoint.\n\nFor §二: `GET /api/v1/tickets/groups/:groupId` → `{ groupId, total, done, pending, status }`. Implementation: scan all runs dirs (root + managers), for each ticket.json read idempotencyKey === groupId; count total; done = tickets whose status is terminal (after cancel projection? \"全部终态才算 settled\"). Need TERMINAL_TICKET_STATUS which includes done/needs_you/failed/idle/aborted. Note canceled tickets: canceled is a projection; a canceled ticket's original status may be \"dispatching\" (non-terminal) but canceled means it's settled? Batch 25 says \"status = 全部终态才算 settled，否则 pending\". Canceled should count as terminal (harness no longer moves it). I'll treat canceled as terminal.\n\nAlso gate by switch `DELEGATION_FANOUT_GROUP` (batch 25 4.4: 沿用批19). When off → 404? Spec says \"开关 DELEGATION_FANOUT_GROUP（沿用批 19）\". Since groupId doesn't exist when off, endpoint should 404 (未启用) — consistent with \"开关关着一个路由都不挂\" convention. I'll mount conditionally (at mount time) — but tests toggle env after mount... The existing test toggles env at runtime for fields. Simpler: always mount, and inside check `fanoutGroupEnabled()` → 404. Hmm, convention in this file: cancel routes mounted conditionally at mount time (`if (delegationCancelEnabled())`). For testability I'll mount always but check inside → returns 404 when off. Document it.\n\n404 also when group doesn't exist. Need to distinguish to return 404: total===0 → 404 `{ok:false,error:\"not_found\"}`.\n\nAlso \"人的消息不等\" (4.3): add comment only.\n\nAlso should the response include tickets? Spec says only `{groupId,total,done,pending,status}`. Keep exactly that (plus ok? spec exact). I'll return `{ ok: true, groupId, total, done, pending, status }`. Hmm \"契约只有一份\" — must update 接口文档.md too. And shared schema? The shared package is for request/event Zod schemas; API response schemas may not exist there. Check for ticket endpoints in shared... probably not. I'll add to 接口文档 only.\n\nNow, is there an existing \"groups\" concept conflict? `/api/v1/tickets/groups/:groupId` — group here means fanout group (requestId), not执事群组 (`/api/v1/groups`). Naming clash noted in comments.\n\nRoute ordering matters: Hono `app.get(\"/api/v1/tickets/:id\")` is registered before; adding `/api/v1/tickets/groups/:groupId` after would be shadowed by `:id` (since \"groups\" would match :id but path has extra segment → no, `/api/v1/tickets/:id` only matches 3 segments; `/api/v1/tickets/groups/xxx` has 4 → no match). So fine. But safer to register before `:id`.\n\nNow §四 pairing details. Let me design concretely:\n\n```ts\nexport function deviceFingerprint(deviceId: string, tokenHash: string): string {\n  const digest = createHash(\"sha256\").update(`lifediary-device-v1|${deviceId}|${tokenHash}`).digest(\"hex\");\n  // 人眼可核：12 位大写十六进制，4-4-4 分组（48 bit，撞库无意义且短）\n  return digest.slice(0, 12).toUpperCase().match(/.{4}/g)!.join(\"-\");\n}\n```\n\nStoredDevice gains:\n- `fingerprint: string`\n- `keyChangedAt?: number`\n\nload(): for each device: compute expected = deviceFingerprint(id, tokenHash). If `fingerprint` absent → set (migration) and mark dirty. If present and !== expected → `keyChangedAt ??= now`, mark dirty. Save if dirty.\n\nSave during load is a bit surprising; but ok. However `load()` is called in constructor; save writes file. If the file is read-only, save throws → constructor throws → server fails to start. Guard with try/catch around save.\n\nverifyDeviceToken: skip if `device.keyChangedAt` (fail-closed). Also, when a token doesn't match any device, nothing.\n\nReturns: `listDevices()` currently strips tokenHash. Now also returns fingerprint + keyChanged boolean. Keep `keyChangedAt` too? Include `keyChanged: boolean` and `keyChangedAt: number|null` for the marker. In index.ts GET /api/v1/pair/devices (the richer one at line 335) add fingerprint/keyChanged. The second duplicate at line 412 returns raw list — update or unify? There are two identical routes registered (line 335 and 412) — Hono uses the first. Leave the second alone (dead) but maybe it's hit? Hono registers both; first wins. I'll update the first only, and note the duplicate exists? Not our scope.\n\nredeem(): include fingerprint in the device record, return `{deviceToken, deviceId, fingerprint}`. index.ts redeem response add `deviceId`, `fingerprint`.\n\nSwitch: `PAIR_DEVICE_FINGERPRINT` default true. When false: don't compute/store fingerprint, don't mark keyChanged, don't include in responses (rollback to today). Implementation: `fingerprintEnabled(env)`.\n\nMigration concern: switch on → old devices get fingerprints written on first load. Switch off → don't touch. If a device has fingerprint stored, switch off → ignore mismatch (no marker). Good.\n\nTests (new file pairing.test.ts, must add to package.json test list):\n1. 指纹可核：格式 `XXXX-XXXX-XXXX`，同设备稳定，不同设备不同；列表不下发 tokenHash。\n2. 键变更：手改 store 文件 tokenHash（模拟键被置换）→ 新实例加载 → keyChanged true，旧 token 验证 false（fail-closed），redeem 新设备仍可用。\n3. 旧记录迁移：无 fingerprint 的旧文件 → 加载后补上且不误判 keyChanged。\n4. 开关 false：列表无 fingerprint 键、篡改不挡（回到今天行为）。\n5. 撤销仍可用。\n\nNeed STORE_PATH env per test — STORE_PATH is read at module load (`const STORE_PATH = process.env...`). So tests must set env before import and use dynamic import with unique paths — but module caches. Since `PairingStore` uses module-level STORE_PATH, one file path per test process. Tests within one file share process → need to reassign? Can't.\n\nOptions: refactor `PairingStore` to accept an optional path in constructor: `constructor(private readonly storePath = STORE_PATH)`. That's a small, justifiable change enabling tests (and doesn't change production behavior). Do it.\n\nNow §一 implementation details + tests. Tests need to import phone-worker and access the transport. Module registers transport at import. In test, `import { phoneTransport } from chancellor` after importing phone-worker gives the registered one. Module state (pending/ready/polls) persists across tests in file, but each test uses unique taskIds, so fine. Need cleanup between tests: cancellations/timeouts will clear. Use unique device names & taskIds.\n\nTest list:\n1. 取消后不发出：dispatch(task, signal) queued; abort; poll → 204.\n2. 超时后不发出：budgetMs 20; wait 40; poll → 204.\n3. 已认领不重复发：poll gets task; second poll (timeoutS=1) → 204 and doesn't get same task.\n4. 取消后结果被丢弃：poll → task; abort; POST result → applied:false (or 404 if entry gone). With new gate: we keep a `discarded` marker? If abort already deleted pending, entry is gone → 404. To make \"丢弃\" explicit, on abort we could keep a short-lived tombstone map `canceled.add(taskId)`; /worker/result then returns 409 {ok:false,error:\"task_canceled\", applied:false} and logs. That's the \"标记\" that makes behavior observable and testable. Tombstones expire with budget? Keep last N (e.g., 200) ids in a Map with timestamps, cleared after 10 min. Reasonable.\n\nHmm, but a canceled task never delivered → phone can't post result. The tombstone matters when abort happens after delivery. Test #4 covers that: poll → delivered → abort → POST result → 409 + applied:false + log. And with switch off → today's 404 unknown_task.\n\n5. 开关旁路：PHONE_ENSURE_ACTIVE=false → after abort, result → 404 (old behavior), and dispatch/poll still works.\n6. 重复 taskId：dispatch same id twice; abort/timeout the first → second still deliverable. (Fix the `finish` identity guard.)\n\nCareful with the promise from dispatch #1 rejecting → handle to avoid unhandled rejection.\n\nLogging: \"[phone] 丢弃迟到结果 task=<id> reason=canceled\" — id only.\n\nAlso §3.3 \"写回前再查一次\" — the actual write-back is chancellor's; server can only decline to resolve. So the result gate = resolution gate. Document honestly in change record: 写回在 chancellor，服务端只能\"不 resolve\"，即不写回.\n\nNow let's also check http-probe.ts to add new endpoints as the requirement says \"新端点进探针\". Let me inspect its structure."
      }
