      "reasoning": "No fanout probe section. I'll add a new section \"· 30. 多副本聚合：GET /tickets/groups/:groupId\" plus a pairing section maybe. Requirements say \"新端点进探针\" — only the group endpoint is a new endpoint. Pairing fingerprint changes existing endpoints; add to probe too? Optional but good: add a small pairing check in probe (devices list has fingerprint). The pairing store path in probe — need isolation `PAIRING_STORE_PATH`. Let me check startServer env doesn't set PAIRING_STORE_PATH — risk of touching real .data/pairing.json. Adding probes that write pairing state would be bad unless isolated. I can add `PAIRING_STORE_PATH: \".data/probe-http-pairing.json\"` to startServer env (safe improvement) and then test redeem → fingerprint. That requires issuing a code via POST /api/v1/pair/code (authenticated; AGENT_TOKEN empty in probe → localhost allowed).\n\nHmm, scope. The requirement lists http probe as verification. I'll add:\n- §30 group aggregation probe (2 replicas, 1 done → pending; all done → settled; unknown → 404).\n- §31 pairing fingerprint probe (device list includes fingerprint; verify matches after redeem; tampering is unit-tested only — don't tamper in probe).\n\nKeep it tight.\n\nNow, before writing code, let me check docs/接口文档.md sections for tickets and pairing to update. Let me find the section numbering.\n\nAlso 变更记录 format examples. And check `docs/基线文档/系统架构.md` for env table location? Requirement says env table in 接口文档 §6. Need to add PHONE_ENSURE_ACTIVE and PAIR_DEVICE_FINGERPRINT there.\n\nLet me view relevant portions of 接口文档.",
