      "reasoning": "Now let me plan the implementation concretely. I'll create a todo list since this is multi-step.\n\nPlan:\n\n**§一 phone-worker.ts**\n- Add `PHONE_ENSURE_ACTIVE` switch (`phoneEnsureActive(env)` exported).\n- Extend PendingEntry: `{ task, resolve, deadlineAt, signal? }`.\n- `pending.delete` guarded by identity.\n- Tombstones: `canceled: Map<string, number>` with TTL 10min, cap 200.\n- `onAbort`: record tombstone before finish.\n- Hand-off gate `nextActiveTask()` (used when switch on): pop ready, skip entries that are gone/expired/aborted (call finish? for expired, the timer will fire; but drop from ready and let timer reject).\n- `flushPoll` uses the gate.\n- `/worker/result`: if switch on and no pending entry: if tombstone → log + `{ok:true, applied:false}` (200? or 409). I'll pick `200 {\"ok\": true, \"applied\": false, \"reason\": \"task_canceled\"}` for canceled and 404 unknown_task otherwise. Hmm, but 200 with applied false on an expired task (tombstone only for cancel) — expired entries removed by timer → 404. Fine.\n- Also before resolving on result, re-check active (not expired/aborted) — if expired: discard, applied:false reason \"task_expired\".\n- Log: `[phone] 丢弃迟到结果 task=<id> reason=<canceled|expired>` (id only).\n\nTests in new `phone-worker.test.ts`:\nUse Hono app with `mountPhoneWorker`, and dispatch via `phoneTransport()` from chancellor (registered by import). But the transport's module-level state is global; tests run sequentially in one file (node:test default concurrency? `test()` at top level runs sequentially unless concurrency option). OK.\n\nBut `registerPhoneTransport` is called at module import; importing phone-worker in test works.\n\nTest 1 cancel before delivery: \n```ts\nconst ac = new AbortController();\nconst p = phoneTransport().dispatch({taskId:\"T1\"...}, ac.signal);\np.catch(()=>{});\nac.abort();\nconst res = await app.request(\"/api/v1/worker/poll\", {method:\"POST\", body: JSON.stringify({timeoutS:1}), headers});\nassert.equal(res.status, 204);\n```\nNeed auth? phone routes mounted directly on a bare Hono app — mountPhoneWorker doesn't add auth, so no headers needed.\n\nTest 2 timeout: dispatch budgetMs 30 → wait 60 → poll → 204. Await rejection.\nTest 3 claimed once: dispatch → poll → task; second poll timeoutS 1 → 204 (1s).\nTest 4 result after cancel: dispatch → poll → task; abort; POST result → 200 applied:false; also assert pending cleared.\nTest 5 switch off: process.env.PHONE_ENSURE_ACTIVE=\"false\"; dispatch → poll → abort → result → 404 unknown_task. Restore env.\nTest 6 duplicate taskId: dispatch A(id X, budget 30), dispatch B(id X, budget 5000). Wait 100ms → A rejects; B must still be deliverable (poll returns taskId X). Then abort B.\n\nCareful: dispatch B overwrites pending[X]; A's timer finish must not delete B's entry (identity guard). But A's `finish` also `ready.splice(indexOf(X))` — if B is in ready at same index, A's cleanup would remove B from ready. Guard: only splice if the entry being finished is the current pending for that id. I'll implement `finish` to only touch shared structures if `pending.get(id) === entry`.\n\nAlso A's timeout rejection must happen. Good.\n\nHmm, `flushPoll` in dispatch: on dispatch B, `flushPoll` may immediately give B to a waiting poll — no polls in test.\n\n**§二 delegation-api.ts**\n- Add pure helper `isTerminalStatus(status, canceled)`.\n- Add route before `/:id`:\n```ts\napp.get(\"/api/v1/tickets/groups/:groupId\", (c) => {...})\n```\nWait — route conflict: `/api/v1/tickets/groups/:groupId` vs `/api/v1/tickets/:id` — Hono matches by path segments; `:id` won't match 4 segments. But registration order: Hono's router (RegExpRouter/TrieRouter) handles static > param anyway. I'll register the group route right before the detail route for clarity.\n\nImplementation:\n```ts\nconst groupId = decodeURIComponent(c.req.param(\"groupId\")).trim();\nif (!fanoutGroupEnabled()) return c.json({ok:false,error:\"not_found\"},404);\nif (!groupId) 404;\nconst workRoot = workRootOf();\nscan root + managers: for each runs dir, store.listTickets(500) → for each row id, readTicketJson → idempotencyKey === groupId.\n```\nBut scanning every ticket.json is O(n) per request; acceptable (limit 300 convention). Use limit 500? Use 300 consistent with others. Hmm, correctness vs perf: use 500 like ticketStats.\n\nNeed canceled set: `storeOf().canceledTicketIds()`.\n\nCount: total, done (terminal or canceled), pending = total - done, status settled if done===total (and total>0).\n\nReturn `{ok:true, groupId, total, done, pending, status}`.\n\n- Tests in delegation-api.test.ts: 3 cases as specified.\n\n**§四 pairing.ts**\n- `deviceFingerprint(deviceId, tokenHash)` exported, `fingerprintEnabled()`, `PairingStore(storePath?)`.\n- StoredDevice: `fingerprint?`, `keyChangedAt?`.\n- load(): migrate/verify; `saveOnLoad` with try/catch.\n- verifyDeviceToken: skip keyChanged devices.\n- listDevices(): return fingerprint + keyChanged (only when switch on; when off omit). `listDevices` return type is `Array<Omit<StoredDevice,\"tokenHash\">>` — with optional fingerprint. When switch off, strip fingerprint and keyChangedAt. Fingerprint is derived from the hash but not reversible — safe to expose either way; but rollback semantics say hide.\n- redeem(): set fingerprint when enabled; return.\n\nindex.ts:\n- redeem response: add `deviceId`, `fingerprint` (when enabled).\n- /api/v1/pair/devices (first): add fingerprint & keyChanged.\n- Second duplicate route at 412: it duplicates; update too? It's unreachable. Leave. Actually Hono may throw on duplicate route? It already exists, so no.\n\nTests: new `pairing.test.ts`, add to package.json test list.\n\n**Probe**: add section 30 (group aggregation) + 31 (pairing fingerprint) and `PAIRING_STORE_PATH` isolation.\n\n**Docs**: 接口文档 §2.9 (new endpoint + group semantics), §5 (fingerprint), §6 (env: PHONE_ENSURE_ACTIVE, PAIR_DEVICE_FINGERPRINT); 变更记录 file.\n\nAlso `docs/基线文档/系统架构.md`? Task says \"契约改接口文档\". New mechanism (phone ensure active) might belong in 系统架构 \"已知边界\"? Keep to 变更记录 + 接口文档, plus maybe a line in 系统架构 about 手机通道. Let me check 系统架构 for phone section later.\n\nSince 批26任务书 is missing, per AGENTS \"契约（新增端点）必须先写方案\". The change record + 接口文档 update serves; but strictly a design doc is required. I'll note the missing task book in the change record and write the design rationale there (it's effectively a small additive endpoint specified by the batch task). I won't create a fake 任务书 file.\n\nLet me start implementing §一.\n\nFirst create tasks.",
