      "reasoning": "Now implement §一 in phone-worker.ts.\n\nKey edits:\n\n1. Add switch function after UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT_MS:\n```ts\n/**\n * 执行前重验开关（2026-11-10 批 26 §一）：默认开。\n * `PHONE_ENSURE_ACTIVE=false` → 交付/收结果都不再复核，回到 2026-11-10 之前的行为（留一行回滚）。\n */\nexport function phoneEnsureActive(env: NodeJS.ProcessEnv = process.env): boolean {\n  const raw = (env.PHONE_ENSURE_ACTIVE ?? \"\").trim().toLowerCase();\n  if (!raw) return true;\n  return raw !== \"false\" && raw !== \"0\" && raw !== \"off\";\n}\n```\n\n2. PendingEntry add deadlineAt, signal.\n3. canceled tombstones map.\n4. finish identity guard.\n\nCurrent finish:\n```ts\nconst finish = (apply) => {\n  if (settled) return;\n  settled = true;\n  clearTimeout(timer);\n  signal?.removeEventListener(\"abort\", onAbort);\n  pending.delete(task.taskId);\n  const queued = ready.indexOf(task.taskId);\n  if (queued >= 0) ready.splice(queued, 1);\n  apply();\n};\n```\nChange to:\n```ts\nconst entry: PendingEntry = {...};\nconst finish = (apply) => {\n  if (settled) return;\n  settled = true;\n  clearTimeout(timer);\n  signal?.removeEventListener(\"abort\", onAbort);\n  // 同 taskId 被重派时，旧单的收尾不能删掉新单的登记（否则新单永远交付不出去）。\n  if (pending.get(task.taskId) === entry) pending.delete(task.taskId);\n  const queued = ready.indexOf(task.taskId);\n  if (queued >= 0) ready.splice(queued, 1);\n  apply();\n};\n```\nBut entry referenced before initialization inside callback — fine since callbacks run later. Need `const entry: PendingEntry = { task, resolve... }` defined before use in finish; but `entry` is assigned before any callback executes (timer created after? finish closure references entry variable; declaration order inside executor: define entry then finish? Let's restructure:\n\n```ts\nreturn new Promise<PhoneResult>((resolve, reject) => {\n  let settled = false;\n  const entry: PendingEntry = {\n    task,\n    deadlineAt: Date.now() + Math.max(1, task.budgetMs),\n    signal,\n    resolve: (result) => finish(() => resolve(result)),\n  };\n  const finish = ... // function declaration hoisted? const finish defined after entry, but entry.resolve calls finish lazily. OK.\n```\nCareful: `entry.resolve` references `finish` before `finish` is initialized, but only at call time → fine.\n\nTS: `const entry` used in `finish` before declaration textually → \"Block-scoped variable 'entry' used before its declaration\"? TS allows use inside a closure defined later? Actually TS errors only on direct use before declaration, not inside function bodies. It's fine.\n\n5. Tombstone recording in onAbort:\n```ts\nconst onAbort = () => {\n  markCanceled(task.taskId);\n  finish(() => reject(abortReason(signal)));\n};\n```\nAnd also for the entry-level: `markCanceled` map TTL.\n\nThe timeout path: no tombstone (unknown_task at 404 is fine; but \"超时后不发出\" is covered at hand-off).\n\n6. Delivery gate:\nReplace `nextQueuedTask()` with:\n\n```ts\nfunction nextQueuedTask(): PhoneTask | null {\n  while (ready.length > 0) {\n    const taskId = ready.shift();\n    if (taskId === undefined) break;\n    const entry = pending.get(taskId);\n    if (!entry) continue;\n    if (phoneEnsureActive()) {\n      const reason = inactiveReason(entry, Date.now());\n      if (reason) {\n        // 已取消 / 已超时：不再交付（取消的单绝不能产生副作用）。\n        dropEntry(taskId);\n        continue;\n      }\n    }\n    return entry.task;\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n```\n\n`inactiveReason(entry, now)`:\n```ts\nexport function inactiveReason(entry: {deadlineAt:number; signal?:AbortSignal}, now: number): \"canceled\" | \"expired\" | null {\n  if (entry.signal?.aborted) return \"canceled\";\n  if (now >= entry.deadlineAt) return \"expired\";\n  return null;\n}\n```\n\n`dropEntry`: remove from pending if same entry, and let its timer/abort settle it. But we only have taskId there. Let me implement inside nextQueuedTask:\n```ts\nif (pending.get(taskId) === entry) pending.delete(taskId);\n```\nBut then the dispatch promise never settles until the timer fires (it will; timer still armed) — expired case timer fires, canceled case abort listener fires. Deleting pending early means result posting gets 404 — fine. However deleting before timer fires means `finish` identity guard won't delete (already gone) — fine, promise still rejects via timer.\n\nActually simpler: don't delete; just skip. But then ready order: we shift it out anyway, so it won't be delivered again. Pending entry stays until timer/abort settles. Cleaner: just `continue` (skip). But if the signal was aborted *without* a listener (undefined signal), no listener → entry stays forever → but we skip it forever; fine, it just leaks until timeout.\n\nHmm, but for a canceled-with-signal task, abort listener already fired and deleted pending & spliced ready. So this branch only triggers for: expired-but-timer-lagged, or aborted-without-listener. Just `continue` is safe and leaves settlement to existing mechanisms. Good, simplest.\n\n7. flushPoll: \n```ts\nfunction flushPoll(task: PhoneTask): boolean { ... poll.resolve(task) }\n```\nDelivery gate already applied in nextQueuedTask before push/dispatch? In dispatch, `if (!flushPoll(task)) ready.push(taskId)`. flushPoll delivers immediately without gate. Add gate there too:\n```ts\nfunction flushPoll(task: PhoneTask): boolean {\n  if (phoneEnsureActive()) {\n    const entry = pending.get(task.taskId);\n    if (!entry || inactiveReason(entry, Date.now())) return false; // 不交出；由 dispatch 放回队列后下次再判\n  }\n  ...\n}\n```\nBut if it returns false due to inactive, dispatch pushes to ready — leaving a stale queued entry. Better: in dispatch, check gate first:\n```ts\nif (phoneEnsureActive() && inactiveReason(entry, Date.now())) {\n   // 刚入队就已失效（signal 在进入前一刻 aborted）：不排队，直接按对应终态收口\n   ...\n}\n```\nThis gets convoluted. Simpler: keep `flushPoll` as is (it's called at dispatch time, when the task was just created and cannot be expired; aborted is checked at dispatch entry). Add the gate only in `nextQueuedTask`, which is the single path for queued tasks. For immediate delivery, check `signal?.aborted` (already at top of dispatch). Good enough.\n\n8. Result path:\n```ts\napp.post(\"/api/v1/worker/result\", async (c) => {\n  ...\n  const entry = pending.get(body.taskId);\n  if (!entry) {\n    if (phoneEnsureActive() && isCanceled(body.taskId)) {\n      console.log(`[phone] 丢弃迟到结果 task=${body.taskId} reason=canceled`);\n      return c.json({ ok: true, applied: false, reason: \"canceled\" });\n    }\n    return c.json({ error: \"unknown_task\" }, 404);\n  }\n  if (phoneEnsureActive()) {\n    const reason = inactiveReason(entry, Date.now());\n    if (reason) {\n      discard: markCanceled? no. log reason, return {ok:true, applied:false, reason}\n    }\n  }\n  ...\n});\n```\nFor expired entry with timer lag: log reason=expired, applied false.\n\nNote: for `applied:false`, should we resolve entry? No — leave it; its timer will reject. Actually if expired but timer hasn't fired, returning applied:false and letting the timer reject is correct (server treats it as idle). Fine.\n\n9. Tombstone helpers:\n```ts\nconst CANCELED_TTL_MS = 10 * 60_000;\nconst CANCELED_CAP = 200;\nconst canceledTasks = new Map<string, number>();\nfunction markCanceled(taskId: string, now = Date.now()): void {\n  canceledTasks.set(taskId, now);\n  if (canceledTasks.size > CANCELED_CAP) {\n    for (const [id, at] of canceledTasks) {\n      if (canceledTasks.size <= CANCELED_CAP) break;\n      if (now - at > CANCELED_TTL_MS) canceledTasks.delete(id);\n    }\n    // 仍然超限：按插入顺序丢最旧的（Map 保序）\n    while (canceledTasks.size > CANCELED_CAP) {\n      const oldest = canceledTasks.keys().next().value;\n      if (oldest === undefined) break;\n      canceledTasks.delete(oldest);\n    }\n  }\n}\nfunction isCanceled(taskId: string, now = Date.now()): boolean {\n  const at = canceledTasks.get(taskId);\n  if (at === undefined) return false;\n  if (now - at > CANCELED_TTL_MS) { canceledTasks.delete(taskId); return false; }\n  return true;\n}\n```\n\nAlso export for tests? `__resetPhoneWorkerState` maybe needed if tests interfere. I'll add a test-only reset guarded by function name `__resetPhoneWorkerStateForTest`. Hmm, AGENTS says avoid over-engineering; but state leakage between tests (pending timers) could confuse. Tests use distinct ids and each test cleans by aborting. I'll add reset only if needed.\n\nAlso export `pendingCount()`? Not needed.\n\nLet me now write the code.",
