        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "Now the result endpoint. Modify the `pending.get` block.\n\nAlso, \"已被别的 worker 认领\" — in nextQueuedTask, a task handed to a poll is removed from ready, so it cannot be handed twice. But if the same taskId was re-pushed (dispatch duplicate with same id), ready may contain id twice; the first poll takes it, the second occurrence remains and could deliver the same id again. Guard: after taking, we shift it out — duplicates remain. To ensure \"已认领不重复发\", track `delivered: Set<string>`? Simpler: when delivering, remove all occurrences of that id from ready:\n\n```ts\nconst idx = ready.indexOf(taskId); while (idx >= 0) { ready.splice(idx,1); ... }\n```\nThat handles duplicate queue entries. I'll add that in nextQueuedTask before returning.\n\nActually the shift already removed the first; then dedupe remaining duplicates:\n```ts\nfor (let i = ready.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) if (ready[i] === taskId) ready.splice(i, 1);\n```\nAdd that.\n\nNow result endpoint."
      }
