        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "Issue: `finish` also splices ready for the taskId — for duplicate dispatch, old finish could remove the new entry from `ready`. Guard it: only splice if pending still points to entry? If pending was overwritten by the new dispatch, the old finish shouldn't touch ready at all. Change:\n\n```ts\nif (pending.get(task.taskId) === entry) {\n  pending.delete(task.taskId);\n  const queued = ready.indexOf(task.taskId);\n  if (queued >= 0) ready.splice(queued, 1);\n}\n```\n\nGood.\n\nAnother issue: `flushPoll` may deliver a task immediately at dispatch. Gate: at dispatch, signal just checked not aborted, deadline is in the future, so fine.\n\nBut `flushPoll` picks first poll regardless of whether the poll's HTTP request was aborted. `onAbort` for poll removes it from polls. Fine.\n\nLet me fix finish."
      }
    ],
