        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "All pass. But note: \"取消后不发出\" takes 1s because poll waits. Could optimize by checking that the task is not in queue — but no queue introspection. Fine.\n\nHowever, there's a subtle issue: the \"取消后不发出\" test would pass even without the new gate (abort listener removes from ready). Same for \"超时后不发出\" (timer removes). So the tests don't actually pin the *new* gate — they pin behavior that existed. The spec asked for these tests anyway. But to \"钉死\" the new code path, I should add a test that hits the gate specifically: an entry in `ready` that is expired but whose timer hasn't fired. Hard to construct without fake timers.\n\nAlternative: `inactiveReason` unit test + a test where abort happens *without* the listener being able to clean ready... Not constructible.\n\nI'll be honest in the change record: the cancel/timeout tests pin end-to-end behavior; the gate itself is covered by the pure `inactiveReason` test. That's acceptable.\n\nHmm, but there's a risk the reviewer says \"tests pass on old code too\". The duplicate-taskId test is genuinely new (would fail before the identity guard). The result-discard test is genuinely new (before: 404, now applied:false). So 2 of 6 pin new behavior. Good enough.\n\nNow run full server test suite? The requirement says per section: typecheck + test. Let me run the full test to be safe, in background while I work on §二? Running tests concurrently with edits can produce confusing failures since tests spawn tsx processes reading files. Better run now (it may take a few minutes).\n\nLet me run it in background and start §二 meanwhile — but editing files while tests run is risky. I'll run full test now and wait."
      }
    ],
