    "rawContent": [
      {
        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "Now add tests. Insert after the existing fanout test in delegation-api.test.ts (line ~481).\n\nTests:\n```ts\ntest(\"多副本聚合：2 个副本 1 个完成 → pending；全完成 → settled；未知组 → 404\", async () => {\n  const root = temp(\"api-groups\");\n  try {\n    const workRoot = join(root, \"runs\");\n    const manager = ensureManager(workRoot, \"agg\");\n    const rootStore = new Store(workRoot);\n    rootStore.saveTicket(makeTicket(\"T-g-a\", workRoot, { idempotencyKey: \"g-1\", status: \"done\" }));\n    rootStore.close();\n    const managerStore = new Store(manager.runs_dir);\n    managerStore.saveTicket(makeTicket(\"T-g-b\", manager.runs_dir, {\n      idempotencyKey: \"g-1\",\n      status: \"working\",\n      options: { dry: true, maxTasks: 8, workRoot: manager.runs_dir, domain: \"agg\" },\n    }));\n    managerStore.close();\n    ...\n```\nWait: does `saveTicket` accept arbitrary status? The Ticket type status is a union? `status: \"dispatching\"` in makeTicket. `status: \"working\"` may not be valid. Use \"dispatching\" for pending. And \"done\" for done.\n\nStore.saveTicket likely writes ticket.json + row. Good.\n\nBody:\n- GET /api/v1/tickets/groups/g-1 → total 2 done 1 pending 1 status pending\n- Create a third? Then update status of T-g-b to done via managerStore.saveTicket again (upsert?). Simpler: create separate group g-2 with two done tickets and assert settled. Or update: `managerStore.updateTicketStatus`? Let me check Store API for status update. Simpler: use another group with both done.\n\n- unknown group → 404.\n- switch off → 404.\n\nAlso check the response includes ok true.\n\nLet me write."
      }
