        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "16 tests pass. Typecheck ran before with 0 errors (the first line was empty output). Let me run the full test suite again at the end. Now §四.\n\nPairing design implementation. Let me write pairing.ts changes.\n\nKey functions:\n\n```ts\n/** 指纹开关（批 26 §四）：默认开；`PAIR_DEVICE_FINGERPRINT=false` → 不呈现 / 不判键变更（回滚）。 */\nexport function deviceFingerprintEnabled(env: NodeJS.ProcessEnv = process.env): boolean {\n  const raw = (env.PAIR_DEVICE_FINGERPRINT ?? \"\").trim().toLowerCase();\n  if (!raw) return true;\n  return raw !== \"false\" && raw !== \"0\" && raw !== \"off\";\n}\n```\n\nFingerprint:\n```ts\n/**\n * 设备指纹（人眼可核）：sha256(deviceId + tokenHash) 取前 12 位十六进制，4-4-4 分组。\n * 只用于\"两台机器上的字符串是否一样\"：48 bit，不可反推令牌，也不当凭据。\n */\nexport function deviceFingerprint(deviceId: string, tokenHash: string): string {\n  const digest = createHash(\"sha256\")\n    .update(`lifediary-device-v1|${deviceId}|${tokenHash}`)\n    .digest(\"hex\")\n    .slice(0, 12)\n    .toUpperCase();\n  return `${digest.slice(0, 4)}-${digest.slice(4, 8)}-${digest.slice(8, 12)}`;\n}\n```\n\nStoredDevice:\n```ts\ninterface StoredDevice {\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n  tokenHash: string;\n  /** 指纹（2026-11-10 批 26 §四）：sha256(id + tokenHash) 的短摘要，人眼可核。 */\n  fingerprint?: string;\n  /** 键被换过（文件里的 tokenHash 与指纹对不上）：该设备的凭据一律 fail-closed。 */\n  keyChangedAt?: number;\n  createdAt: number;\n  lastSeenAt?: number;\n  revokedAt?: number;\n}\n```\n\nPairingStore constructor:\n```ts\nexport class PairingStore {\n  private store: Store;\n  constructor(private readonly storePath: string = STORE_PATH) {\n    this.store = load(this.storePath, ...);\n    ...\n  }\n```\nload currently reads STORE_PATH. Change signature `load(storePath: string)` and `save(store: Store)` → `save(storePath, store)`.\n\nThen in constructor:\n```ts\nconstructor(private readonly storePath: string = STORE_PATH) {\n  this.store = load(storePath);\n  if (deviceFingerprintEnabled()) this.sealFingerprints();\n}\n```\n\n`sealFingerprints()`:\n```ts\nprivate sealFingerprints(now = Date.now()): void {\n  let dirty = false;\n  for (const device of this.store.devices) {\n    const expected = deviceFingerprint(device.id, device.tokenHash);\n    if (device.fingerprint === undefined) {\n      device.fingerprint = expected;\n      dirty = true;\n      continue;\n    }\n    if (!hashEquals(device.fingerprint, expected) && device.keyChangedAt === undefined) {\n      // 键被换过（文件被改 / 从别的机器搬来）：标记而不是静默重绑。\n      device.keyChangedAt = now;\n      console.warn(`[pairing] 设备 ${device.id.slice(0, 8)} 的凭据指纹不匹配，已按 fail-closed 停用`);\n      dirty = true;\n    }\n  }\n  if (dirty) this.persist();\n}\n```\n\n`persist()` wraps save in try/catch to not break startup:\n```ts\nprivate persist(): void {\n  try { save(this.storePath, this.store); }\n  catch (error) { console.warn(...); }\n}\n```\n\nCareful: fingerprint comparison with hashEquals is fine (equal-length hex). Use `!==` simpler and no timing concern (not a secret comparison). I'll use `!==`.\n\nverifyDeviceToken: skip `if (device.keyChangedAt) continue;`.\n\nAlso note: when key changed, `lastSeenAt` not touched.\n\nredeem: when enabled, set `fingerprint: deviceFingerprint(device.id, device.tokenHash)`.\n\nlistDevices: currently returns rest (minus tokenHash). Add mapping:\n```ts\nlistDevices(): Array<Omit<StoredDevice, \"tokenHash\">> {\n  const on = deviceFingerprintEnabled();\n  return this.store.devices.map(({ tokenHash: _hidden, ...rest }) => {\n    if (!on) {\n      const { fingerprint: _f, keyChangedAt: _k, ...legacy } = rest;\n      return legacy;\n    }\n    return rest;\n  });\n}\n```\nType: `Omit<StoredDevice,\"tokenHash\">` includes optional fingerprint/keyChangedAt, so returning legacy is fine.\n\nAlso when fingerprint is disabled, `sealFingerprints` isn't called → legacy devices have no fingerprint. If a device was sealed while enabled and then switch disabled, list strips it.\n\nRedeemResult add `fingerprint?: string`.\n\nindex.ts updates:\n- redeem response: `deviceId: result.deviceId, ...(result.fingerprint ? {fingerprint: result.fingerprint} : {})`.\n- devices list mapping: add `fingerprint: device.fingerprint ?? null, keyChanged: Boolean(device.keyChangedAt)`.\n- The second duplicate devices route returns raw list — it's shadowed; leave but maybe update to avoid confusion? Leave.\n\nTests `pairing.test.ts`:\n```ts\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport { mkdtempSync, readFileSync, rmSync, writeFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { tmpdir } from \"node:os\";\nimport { join } from \"node:path\";\nimport { test } from \"node:test\";\nimport { PairingStore, deviceFingerprint } from \"./pairing.ts\";\n```\n\nTest 1: \n```ts\nconst path = join(temp, \"pairing.json\");\nconst store = new PairingStore(path);\nconst code = store.issueCode().code;\nconst redeemed = store.redeem(code, \"测试机\");\nassert.notEqual(typeof redeemed, \"string\");\nconst result = redeemed as RedeemResult;\nassert.match(result.fingerprint!, /^[0-9A-F]{4}-[0-9A-F]{4}-[0-9A-F]{4}$/);\nassert.equal(result.fingerprint, deviceFingerprint(result.deviceId, sha? )) \n```\nWe don't know tokenHash, but fingerprint must equal recomputation from file:\n```ts\nconst file = JSON.parse(readFileSync(path,\"utf8\"));\nconst stored = file.devices[0];\nassert.equal(result.fingerprint, deviceFingerprint(stored.id, stored.tokenHash));\n```\nAnd `store.verifyDeviceToken(result.deviceToken)` true; listDevices has no tokenHash; fingerprint present; keyChanged falsy.\n\nTest 2 (key change): tamper file: set devices[0].tokenHash = sha256(\"other\") (import createHash). Then `new PairingStore(path)` → `verifyDeviceToken(originalToken)` false; listDevices()[0].keyChangedAt number; fingerprint unchanged (sealed mismatch → keyChangedAt). Also second load keeps keyChangedAt (idempotent, doesn't reset).\n\nTest 3 (legacy migration): write a store file without fingerprint → new PairingStore → list has fingerprint, no keyChangedAt, verify true.\n\nTest 4 (switch off): process.env.PAIR_DEVICE_FINGERPRINT=\"false\"; new PairingStore(path with tampered hash) → verifyDeviceToken(original) — hmm with switch off, keyChangedAt may already be set in file from test 2. Use a fresh file. With switch off: redeem → no fingerprint; list items lack fingerprint/keyChangedAt keys; tampering isn't detected (verify returns false anyway because hash mismatch — that's inherent). The observable difference: no marker and no fingerprint. Assert `\"fingerprint\" in device === false`.\n\nCareful: env var read at call time (deviceFingerprintEnabled reads process.env each call) — good for tests.\n\nNote: PairingStore loads in constructor; if switch off but file has fingerprints, they're preserved.\n\nAlso: when key changed is detected, do we keep `tokenHash` as-is? Yes (never overwrite); verification refuses. Revoke works.\n\nEdge: `MAX_DEVICES` filter drops revoked, and on redeem it rebuilds devices from existing → keyChangedAt preserved.\n\nNow implement."
      }
    ],
