        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "All 4 pass. Now run the whole test suite (typecheck + test) for §四 completion. Then the probe and docs.\n\nBut first: the probe sections. Let me add to http-probe:\n1. In startServer env, add `PAIRING_STORE_PATH: \".data/probe-http-pairing.json\"`.\n2. A group aggregation section after §18 ticket fixtures. Insert near the ticket section end (~line 1750?) — but the store is closed. I can add fixture tickets with idempotencyKey and query.\n\nLet me look at where §18 ends and where to insert §30. I'll add at the end of the probe before cleanup, but the server at that time may be a later server instance with different workRoot. Simpler: add group aggregation right after §18 assertions (same server, same TICKETS_ROOT) by seeding two tickets with idempotencyKey \"probe-g-1\" (one done, one dispatching) and one \"probe-g-2\" both done.\n\nWhere exactly? After the ticket fixtures are saved (line 1591) and before assertions... The store is closed at 1591. I can reopen a Store to save extra fixtures before assertions, or include them in the initial fixture block. Add to the initial block:\n\n```ts\n// 多副本聚合（批 26 §二）：同 requestId 的两张，一张终态一张在办。\nstore.saveTicket(fixture(\"T-group-a\", { idempotencyKey: \"probe-group-1\", status: \"done\" }));\nstore.saveTicket(fixture(\"T-group-b\", { idempotencyKey: \"probe-group-1\" }));\nstore.saveTicket(fixture(\"T-group-c\", { idempotencyKey: \"probe-group-2\", status: \"done\" }));\nstore.saveTicket(fixture(\"T-group-d\", { idempotencyKey: \"probe-group-2\", status: \"failed\" }));\n```\n\nThen assertions after the ticketsJson block:\n\n```ts\n// ── 18.5 多副本聚合 ──\nconst groupPending = await (await fetch(`${BASE}/api/v1/tickets/groups/probe-group-1`)).json();\ncheck(groupPending.total===2 && groupPending.done===1 && groupPending.pending===1 && groupPending.status===\"pending\", ...)\nconst groupSettled = ...\nconst groupUnknown = await fetch(.../groups/nope); check(status 404)\n```\n\nNote: fixtures with status \"done\"/\"failed\" — valid statuses.\n\n3. Pairing fingerprint probe: needs a device. Steps:\n- GET /api/v1/pair/devices → check each device has fingerprint (may be empty list initially).\n- POST /api/v1/pair/redeem with a fresh code: need a code. With AGENT_TOKEN=\"\" and loopback allowed, POST /api/v1/pair/code returns {code}. Then redeem with deviceName. Then GET devices → find by id? Redeem response now has deviceId + fingerprint. Check fingerprint format and that devices list contains it.\n- Then cleanup: revoke the device (so repeated probe runs don't accumulate; MAX_DEVICES 32 anyway). And delete `.data/probe-http-pairing.json` at cleanup.\n\nWhere to put? Near the end (after §29) since it starts a fresh server? Actually pair endpoints require the same server instance; any instance works. Add as §30 at the end, before cleanup, using the current `server`/`BASE`.\n\nLet me find the end of the file/cleanup section."
      }
