    "rawContent": [
      {
        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "Now the pairing fingerprint probe section at the end (after §29) and env isolation.\n\nAdd `PAIRING_STORE_PATH: \".data/probe-http-pairing.json\"` in startServer env, plus cleanup rm.\n\nThen §30:\n```ts\nconsole.log(\"\\n· 30. 配对设备指纹（批 26 §四）\");\nconst pairCode = (await (await fetch(`${BASE}/api/v1/pair/code`, {method:\"POST\"})).json()) as {code?: string};\nconst redeemed = await fetch(`${BASE}/api/v1/pair/redeem`, {method:\"POST\", headers, body: JSON.stringify({code: pairCode.code, deviceName: \"探针手机\"})});\nconst redeemedBody = ...\ncheck(/^[0-9A-F]{4}-.../.test(redeemedBody.fingerprint), \"redeem 下发人眼可核指纹\", ...)\ncheck(typeof redeemedBody.deviceId === \"string\", ...)\nconst devices = (await fetch(`${BASE}/api/v1/pair/devices`)).json();\nconst mine = devices.devices.find(d=>d.id===redeemedBody.deviceId)\ncheck(mine?.fingerprint === redeemedBody.fingerprint, \"设备清单同一指纹\")\ncheck(!(\"tokenHash\" in mine), \"清单不含哈希\")\n// 撤销，免得反复跑累积\nawait fetch(`${BASE}/api/v1/pair/devices/${deviceId}/revoke`, {method:\"POST\"});\n```\nNote: /api/v1/pair/code requires auth; with AGENT_TOKEN=\"\" the probe server allows loopback (auth middleware). The probe's fetch goes to 127.0.0.1 — but is there cookie/token requirement? `createAuthMiddleware(null, ...)` → loopback allowed. Yes.\n\nWait: at the end of the probe, the last server was started with `{ COMPANIONS_ENABLED: \"true\", AGENT_BASH_BG_TIMEOUT: \"\" }` via startServer which sets AGENT_TOKEN: \"\" — good.\n\nNote the pairing store file persists between probe runs; each run adds a device then revokes. Max 32 anyway. Cleanup rm at finally.\n\nWhere exactly to insert §30: after the `bgOff` check at 2728, before `} finally {`.\n\nLet me do the edits."
      }
    ],
