      {
        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "Aha: `tickets.idempotency_key` is UNIQUE per DB. My fixtures T-group-a and T-group-b both have idempotencyKey \"probe-group-1\" in the *same* store (TICKETS_ROOT) → UNIQUE violation. That's why the earlier run failed too (masked by cleanup error).\n\nThe batch-19 test noted: same requestId replicas are in different runs dirs because same DB has unique key. So put one of each group in the manager dir.\n\nAdjust: T-group-a in root (probe-group-1, done), T-group-b in domain dir (probe-group-1). T-group-c root (probe-group-2 done), T-group-d domain (probe-group-2 failed).\n\nThe domain store is created later (line ~1600). I'll move b/d saves there.\n\nLet me edit: remove T-group-b/T-group-d from root block; add to domainStore block."
      }
